Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: ipad5: Enable the AOP sensors

Enable the always-on processor and its mailbox on the iPad 5 with its
AOP firmware, which brings up the accelerometer, gyroscope and pressure
sensor. Apple's BuildManifest gives every iPad 5 model (J71s, J71t,
J72s, J72t) the same AOP firmware, aopfw-ipad6faop, so this goes in the
shared iPad 5 file.

The A9's AOP firmware reports the accelerometer in its sensor frame:
the device frame negated, so that flat, screen up reads z = -1 g and
upright y = -1 g. Give the accelerometer the mount-matrix that maps it
for desktops in the shared iPad 5 file, so every iPad 5 model has it
once its AOP firmware is known.

[Orchard: from orchard PR #101, commit a54e2049; the J71t part of
 devices/s8000/0007 without the reserved shutdown page and the
 apple,certified-reload, memory-region, apple,observe-domains and
 apple,spi0-domain properties; the AOP enable and the mount-matrix moved
 from the J71t board file to the shared iPad 5 file]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
index fc06d53..8015872 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
@@ -139,6 +139,28 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/* All iPad 5 models use the same AOP firmware (ipad6faop). */
+&aop {
+	firmware-name = "apple/aop-ipad6f.bin", "apple/aop-ipad6f-ext.bin";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&aop_mbox {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/*
+ * The AOP reports the accelerometer in its sensor frame, which is the
+ * device frame (x right, y up, z out of the screen) negated: flat, screen up
+ * reads z = -1 g, upright y = -1 g. iio-sensor-proxy takes upright as
+ * negative y and needs z flipped.
+ */
+&aop_accel {
+	mount-matrix = "1", "0", "0",
+		       "0", "1", "0",
+		       "0", "0", "-1";
+};
+
 &framebuffer0 {
 	power-domains = <&ps_disp0 &ps_dp>;
 };
